{{{{{1<noinclude>|Ability data</noinclude>}}}|Friend of the Forest|{{{2|}}}|{{{3|}}}|{{{4|}}}|{{{5|}}}
|champion     = Ivern
|skill        = I
|icon         = Friend of the Forest.png
|blurbicon    = Friend of the Forest.png
|blurb        = {{sbc|Innate:}} {{ci|Ivern}} cannot attack nor damage non-epic {{tip|monsters}}. When he targets a jungle camp, he {{tip|channel|plants}} a magical {{as|grove|buzzword2}} under it at the cost of {{as|health}} and {{as|mana}}.
|blurb2       = The {{as|grove|buzzword2}} charges up over time to fully mature, upon which '''Ivern''' can then target the monsters to instantly clear the camp. Using {{si|Smite}} on a monster in the {{as|grove|buzzword2}} will clear the camp regardless of maturity. 
|description = {{sbc|Innate:}} '''Ivern''' cannot attack nor damage non-epic {{tip|monster|monsters}}. Instead, targeting a jungle camp initiates a {{fd|2.5}} second {{tip|channel}} that will plant a {{as|grove|buzzword2}} upon the camp. Placing a {{as|grove|buzzword2}} costs {{sti|health|{{as|{{pplevel|(15-(x-1)*0.882)/100*({{ccd|Ivern|hp_base}}+{{ccd|Ivern|hp_lvl}}*(x-1)*(0.7025+0.0175*(x-1)))|formula = (15% - 0.882% per level after 1) of base health}} health}}}} and {{sti|mana|{{as|{{pplevel|(20-(x-1)*1.175)/100*({{ccd|Ivern|mp_base}}+{{ccd|Ivern|mp_lvl}}*(x-1)*(0.7025+0.0175*(x-1)))|formula = (20% - 1.175% per level after 1) of base mana}} mana}}}}. The channel cannot be cancelled in the first {{fd|0.15}} seconds and in the last {{fd|0.5}} seconds.
|description2 = '''''Ivern''' cannot place a grove while he is affected by {{tip|cast-inhibiting crowd control}} or a {{tip|lockout}} that disables abilities.''
|description3 = The {{as|grove|buzzword2}} matures over {{pp|40;38;36;34;32;30;27;24;21;18;15;11;7;3;1|formula = 42 - 2 per level until level 6, then 3 until level 11, then 4 until level 15. ''This is capped at 1 second at level 15.''}} seconds. When fully matured, '''Ivern''' can target the camp again to ''free'' it after a {{fd|0.5}}-second [[cast time]], clearing the camp and receiving the {{tt|{{g|full gold}} and {{sti|experience|{{as|full experience}}}}|Not full when freeing Krug camp, see notes}} [[bounty|bounties]]. Using {{si|Smite}} on a monster within the {{as|grove|buzzword2}} will instantly ''free'' the camp regardless of maturity.
|description4 = If the camp's large monster has already been slain prior to planting a {{as|grove|buzzword2}}, '''Ivern''' will ''free'' the camp upon completing the channel at no cost. Similarly, the {{as|grove|buzzword2}} will instantly mature if the large monster is slain.
|targeting    = Unit
|affects      = Monsters
|silence      = true
|notes        = 
* Freeing the {{ui|Ancient Krug|Krug camp}} will only grant the {{g|gold}} and {{sti|{{as|experience}}}} of 1 {{ui|Ancient Krug}}, 2 {{ui|Krug|Krugs}}, and 3 {{ui|Krug|Mini Krugs}}.
* '''Ivern''' must be within {{tip|er|icononly = true}} 275 units of the {{tt|large monster|if still alive}} of the targeted camp to start channeling or collect a {{as|grove|buzzword2}}. The large monsters also must be {{tip|sight|visible}}.
* If '''Ivern''' cannot afford the cost to place a grove, ''Friend of the Forest'' is placed on a cooldown equal to the number of seconds it takes for his {{as|{{sti|health regeneration}}}} and/or {{as|{{sti|mana regeneration}}}} to restore him to the amount of health and/or mana needed to afford the cost.
** The cooldown will update based on '''Ivern's''' '''current''' health and mana regeneration, as well as his '''current''' health and mana.
* If '''Ivern's''' level is 19 or higher, he will be {{tip|heal|healed}} and receive {{as|mana}} when placing a {{as|grove|buzzword2}}.
* ''Friend of the Forest'' can be used while '''Ivern''' or the camp is in combat and, once the {{as|grove|buzzword2}} is placed, {{si|Smite}} can be used to instantly claim the camp. {{tip|Interrupt|Interrupting}} '''Ivern's''' channel is the only way to contest jungle camps, short of killing the camp during the channel time.
* Freeing a {{as|grove|buzzword2}} causes the monsters within the camp to be dealt {{as|5000 true damage}} in the {{tip|raw damage|internalraw damage}} source type by '''Ivern''', despite his inability to damage them.
* ''Friend of the Forest'' will leave '''Ivern''' at {{as|1 health}} if cast with exactly the required amount. ''Friend of the Forest'' cannot be cast with less, unlike other abilities with health costs.
* Non-epic monsters can attack '''Ivern''' if his allies enter combat with the monster and he manages to receive aggro.{{bug}}
** {{ui|Voidmite|Voidmites}} uses the allied healthbar-colours whilst still being able to be damaged by '''Ivern'''.{{bug}}
* The following table refers for interactions while '''Ivern''' is {{tip|channel|channeling}}:
** '''Ivern''' is unable to act during the first {{fd|0.15}} and last {{fd|0.5}} seconds of the channel.
